; atleast_integer_model: ATLEAST on an integer {0, 1, 2} model raises NonBinaryModel.
;
; ATLEAST writes the penalty for at least one of x0, x1, x2, and spec/xqvm/HLF.md derives
; every constraint expansion under x^2 = x, which holds only for binary
; variables. On any other domain the same terms encode a different penalty,
; so spec/xqvm/ISA.md has ATLEAST raise NonBinaryModel instead. Every other
; operand is valid, so the domain check alone decides.

PUSH 4
PUSH 3
XQMX r0          ; integer model, k = 3, 4 variables
VECI r1          ; indices [0, 1, 2]
PUSH 0
VECPUSH r1
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r1
PUSH 2
VECPUSH r1
PUSH 1           ; k
PUSH 1           ; penalty
ATLEAST r0 r1
HALT
